    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass with a green build. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Change\n\nOn successful owner create, the pipeline now enqueues a welcome notification via the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueOwnerWelcome.java`\n\nFollows the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern: a single public `service` method reads the saved owner (`@Val Owner`) and emits one line via a `NOTIFY`-named SLF4J logger carrying the owner id and memberId:\n\n```java\nprivate static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n}\n```\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`\n\nInserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `recordIdempotency`, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]`. Placing it after `save` and `assignMemberId` guarantees both the persisted owner id and assigned memberId are available.\n\nPlacement matters: it runs only on the success path (after `save`/`audit`), so rejected creates (400/409 escalations that short-circuit earlier) emit nothing \u2014 matching \"on successful create.\"\n\nThe target `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes (the captured line `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` contains both the id and memberId), and the full suite is green (255 tests, 0 failures).",
